<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch West India Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1621">1621</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Geoctroyeerde Westindische Compagnie, GWC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Company was a chartered company established in 1621 to conduct Dutch trade and warfare in the Atlantic. It played a central role in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>'s activities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>, though it struggled financially and was later reorganised.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company.jpg" alt="Dutch West India Company" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flag_of_the_Dutch_West_India_Company.png: *Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg: Zscout370 derivative work: Fentener van Vliss... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dutch_West_India_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
